      "title": "Cyclone Arnab stalls off India, prolonging rain and flood threat",
      "content_html": "Cyclone Arnab’s slow, near-stationary approach to India’s Andhra Pradesh coast prolonged the landfall process and heightened the risk of extreme rain and flash flooding, Down To Earth reported. The storm crossed the southeastern coast on Wednesday, Oct. 28, after forming over the Bay of Bengal. The India Meteorological Department (IMD) warned that its slow movement could keep drawing moisture from the sea.\n\nThe weather bureau recorded 217 millimetres of rain in Visakhapatnam and warned of flash flooding across coastal Andhra Pradesh and nearby regions through late Wednesday. Several reports linked the unusually intense storm season to El Niño and warming. Swiss public broadcaster RTS also reported that scientists say climate change amplifies El Niño’s effects.",
